That matches! The color mode in settings was set to 'bw' but the calculateSheets function only makes it B/W when `colorMode === 'color'`, not when it's 'bw'. Actually looking at the code:

```js
const isColorMode = settings.colorMode === 'color';
if (isColorMode) {
  return { totalSheets, colorSheets: totalSheets, bwSheets: 0 };
}
const colorRatio = totalPages > 0 ? colorPages / totalPages : 0;
const colorSheets = Math.ceil(totalSheets * colorRatio);
```

So when colorMode is 'bw', it still calculates color sheets based on the ratio from the file analysis. Since the file is 100% color (1 color page out of 1), the ratio is 1.0, so all sheets are color. This is actually the expected behavior - 'bw' doesn't force B/W in this implementation, it's 'auto' that detects, and 'color' forces all color. The 'bw' should probably force B/W.

Actually wait, let me re-read the pricing service. Looking at `calculateSheets`:
```js
const isColorMode = settings.colorMode === 'color';
if (isColorMode) {
  return { totalSheets, colorSheets: totalSheets, bwSheets: 0 };
}
// auto/bw mode: calculate based on ratio
const colorRatio = totalPages > 0 ? colorPages / totalPages : 0;
```

So when `colorMode` is 'bw', it falls through to the ratio-based calculation. This means if a file has color pages, even in 'bw' mode, some sheets will be counted as color. That seems like a bug - 'bw' should force all sheets to be B/W.

Let me fix the calculateSheets function.

