Now I see the bug clearly. Lines 211-217:

```js
const pages = JSON.parse(printJob.pages || '[]');
if (pages.length > 0) {
    const totalPdfPages = pages.length;
    if (totalPdfPages > 0) {
        options.pages = pages.map(p => p + 1).join(',');
    }
}
```

This takes the ORIGINAL page numbers (0-indexed) and converts them to 1-indexed for `pdf-to-printer`. But the PDF has been processed by `processPDF` which already EXTRACTED only those pages into a new PDF. So the new PDF only has pages [1, 2, 3, ...] sequentially, not the original page numbers.

For example:
