So the file is found from `order.files` using `printJob.fileId`. The settings come from the print job, not the file. The `file` object is the `OrderFile` record from the order's `files` relation.

But wait - in my test, I create the print job AFTER the order, so when `processAndDispatchOrder` queries the order, it will include the newly created print job. The file was created as part of the order, so `order.files` will contain it.

This should work. But there's a subtle issue: I use `require('./src/services/printProcessor')` in the loop, and `require` is cached by Node.js. So the first call will cache the module, and subsequent calls will use the same module. This should be fine since the module is loaded once.

Let me run the test.

