Now serve the superadmin app at /superadmin. Add before the catch-all (which is now after my super admin routes). The catch-all `app.get('*')` needs to exclude /superadmin. Since the superadmin static will be registered BEFORE the catch-all, and express matches in order, `/superadmin` path requests will hit the static middleware first. But SPA deep links within superadmin (e.g., /superadmin/shops) need a fallback to its index.html. I'll add:

```js
const SUPERADMIN_DIST = path.join(__dirname, '..', '..', 'superadmin', 'dist');
if (fs.existsSync(SUPERADMIN_DIST)) {
  app.use('/superadmin', express.static(SUPERADMIN_DIST));
  app.get('/superadmin/*', (req, res) => {
    res.sendFile(path.join(SUPERADMIN_DIST, 'index.html'));
  });
}
```

