Now update seed.js to create the super admin. And ensure subscriptions for the demo shop. The seed skips if shops exist — but I want the super admin to always exist. I'll add a super-admin ensure step at the TOP of seed main() (before the skip), so it runs even when DB already seeded. That way after deploy, super admin exists.

Super admin credentials: email `superadmin@patelautoprint.com`, password from env `SUPER_ADMIN_PASSWORD` or default. I'll default to `superadmin123` and log clearly. Also add subscription for demo shop when creating it.

Let me edit seed.js:
1. At start of main(), after dedup, ensure super admin exists:
```js
const superAdminEmail = 'superadmin@patelautoprint.com';
const superAdminPassword = process.env.SUPER_ADMIN_PASSWORD || 'superadmin123';
let sa = await prisma.user.findFirst({ where: { email: superAdminEmail } });
if (!sa) {
  const hash = await bcrypt.hash(superAdminPassword, 10);
  sa = await prisma.user.create({ data: { shopId: null, email: superAdminEmail, passwordHash: hash, name: 'Super Admin', role: 'SUPER_ADMIN' } });
  console.log(`Super admin created: ${superAdminEmail}`);
} 
```
Note User.shopId now optional — good.

2. When creating demo shop, also create subscription.

