The user wants to restrict the Razorpay checkout to UPI apps only (Google Pay, PhonePe, Paytm), and disable cards and netbanking.

In Razorpay, this is done via the checkout options:
- `method` option: set `method: { upi: {} }` to show only UPI, or
- `hide` option: `hide: { netbanking: true, card: true, wallet: true, bank_transfer: true }`
- For UPI apps, you can set `config: { display: { blocks: { upi: { name: ..., instruments: [...] } } } }`

Actually, the Razorpay Checkout API options are passed at checkout time (frontend). The backend initiates the order — the method restrictions are a frontend concern (in `razorpay.checkout` options).

Let me find the frontend checkout code. The initiate response had `upiIntent: true` — there's a `upiIntent` flag. Let me look at the frontend payment modal code.

The frontend uses Razorpay's checkout.js. To restrict payment methods:
```js
var options = {
  key: ...,
  order_id: ...,
  ...
  hide: {
    netbanking: true,
    card: true,
    wallet: true,
    bank_transfer: true
  }
}
```

Or to show only UPI apps:
```js
method: {
  upi: {}
}
```

For UPI apps specifically (Google Pay, PhonePe, Paytm), when the user selects UPI, they see a list of UPI apps. Razorpay handles the "saved UPI apps" — but you can also add specific UPI apps via the UPI link option or `config.display.blocks`:

```js
config: {
  display: {
    blocks: {
      upi: {
        name: 'UPI Apps',
        instruments: [
          { method: 'upi', source: 'collect' }  // ...
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Actually the simplest robust approach: use `hide: { netbanking, card, wallet, bank_transfer, vpa }` and `method: { upi: {} }`. When `method.upi` is set, the checkout shows only UPI. The UPI section will show the "enter UPI ID" option plus apps if Razorpay detects them on the device.

Actually, let me recall exactly. Razorpay Checkout options:
- `method`: { upi: {} } — "Set upi: {} to show only UPI payment methods."
- `hide`: { netbanking: true, card: true, wallet: true, upi: true, bank_transfer: true, vpa: true } — hide specific methods.

To show ONLY UPI apps (Google Pay, PhonePe, Paytm) — Razorpay shows the UPI apps section automatically when the device has apps installed; but on desktop it shows a list of "Google Pay, PhonePe, Paytm, etc." with VPA entry. There's a way to prefill/pre-select UPI apps:

```js
method: {
  upi: {}
},
config: {
  display: {
    blocks: {
      upi: {
        name: 'Other UPI Apps',
        instruments: [
          { method: 'upi', source: 'collect', flows: { qr: true, intent: true } }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Hmm, this is getting complicated. The key user requirement: they want Google Pay, PhonePe, Paytm UPI apps only, no cards, no netbanking.

