    ],
  },
  method: { upi: {} },
  hide: { netbanking: true, card: true, wallet: true, bank_transfer: true, emi: true, pay_later: true },
  handler: async (response) => { await verifyRazorpayPayment(orderId, response.razorpay_payment_id); },
  modal: { ondismiss: () => {...} },
  theme: { color: '#1976d2' },
};
```

I'm slightly unsure about the exact `intents` type strings. Let me verify quickly via web search to avoid a wrong option. Actually, the "Best Practices" section I read says the intent page lists apps automatically in order GPAY > PhonePe > Paytm > BHIM. So even without `intents`, it lists them. But adding `intents` pins them. The format `{ type: 'google_pay', flow: 'intent' }` — I've seen this in Razorpay docs for the checkout `upi` option. Let me do a quick web search to confirm.

Let me also consider whether to pass customer contact to backend `payment/initiate` so notes include it — nice-to-have, skip to minimize risk.

