Now implement cover+clip in the n>1 branch of `createContactSheet` in all 3 files. Design:

```js
const {
  pushGraphicsState, popGraphicsState, moveTo, lineTo, closePath, clip, endPath,
} = require('pdf-lib'); // already have PDFDocument — destructure at top requires... 
```
Wait — each file imports `{ PDFDocument } = require('pdf-lib')` at top. I'll destructure operators there too.

New inner loop:
```js
for (let j = 0; j < chunk.length; j++) {
  const col = j % cols;
  const rowFromTop = Math.floor(j / cols);
  try {
    const embedded = await embedImage(newDoc, chunk[j].path);
    const imgW = embedded.width || cellW;
    const imgH = embedded.height || cellH;
    const boxW = cellW - margin * 2;
    const boxH = cellH - margin * 2;
    // Cover: scale to fill the cell (crop overflow) so the sheet has no white gaps
    const scale = Math.max(boxW / imgW, boxH / imgH);
    const drawW = imgW * scale;
    const drawH = imgH * scale;
    const x = col * cellW + (cellW - drawW) / 2;
    const y = dims.h - (rowFromTop + 1) * cellH + (cellH - drawH) / 2;
    const clipX = col * cellW + margin;
    const clipY = dims.h - (rowFromTop + 1) * cellH + margin;
    page.pushOperators(
      pushGraphicsState(),
      moveTo(clipX, clipY),
      lineTo(clipX + boxW, clipY),
      lineTo(clipX + boxW, clipY + boxH),
      lineTo(clipX, clipY + boxH),
      closePath(),
      clip(),
      endPath()
    );
    page.drawImage(embedded, { x, y, width: drawW, height: drawH });
    page.pushOperators(popGraphicsState());
  } catch (err) { ... }
}
```

Important: does `page.pushOperators(...)` then `page.drawImage(...)` then `pushOperators(pop)` maintain ORDER in content stream? drawImage appends operators to the same content stream via node... pdf-lib PDFPage.drawImage uses `this.node.wrapContentOperators`? Hmm — pdf-lib PDFPage methods push to `this.node` content stream via `addContentStream`? Actually pdf-lib PDFPage keeps `_contentStream`... In pdf-lib, PDFPage.drawImage → `this.node.addOperator(...)`? PDFPage has `pushOperators(...ops)` API: "Pushes the given operators onto the page's content stream". And drawImage internally: `this.node.drawImage(...)`? PDFPageLeaf? Let me check how drawImage composes operators — whether it appends to same stream in call order.

pdf-lib source (api/PDFPage.ts): drawImage calls `const xObject = ...; this.node.setXObjects(...); const matrix = ...; this.contentStream...`? Actually PDFPage has `getContentStream()` — drawX methods get/create `this.contentStream` and push operators; `pushOperators` ALSO uses same content stream: 
```ts
public pushOperators(...operators: PDFOperator[]) {
  const contentStream = this.getContentStream();
  contentStream.push(...operators);
}
```
and drawImage:
```ts
const xObject = ...;
this.node.setXObject(...)
const contentStream = this.getContentStream();
contentStream.push(...drawImage(...))  // something like that
```
Same contentStream, push order = call order ✓. So sequence q W n [draw] Q ✓.

